  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/psyc100-500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Psyc 401.01 Expiration of License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Psyc 401.01 Expiration of License.\n\n(a) A license to practice psychology shall automatically expire on the last day of the month which is 2 years from the date issued by the board.\n\n(b) An expired license shall not be renewed, but upon application, may be reinstated in accordance with Psyc 401.05.\n\n(c) If a license has expired pursuant to Psyc 401.01 (a), the licensee shall not engage in the practice of psychology until such time as a new or reinstated license has been granted by the board.\n\nSource. #12035-B, eff 11-4-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/psyc100-500.html"
